  "recap": "The Base Invaders outlasted the Marinaders 30–25 on Monday, August 17, in a slugfest that saw both offenses swinging hot bats all game long. The Invaders piled up 38 hits and got 11 different players on base, with the bats simply outpacing the Marinaders down the stretch for the 5-run win. Jason had a night to remember, going a perfect 6-for-6 with 4 RBI and 2 home runs, while Brendan backed him up with a 4-for-4 performance of his own, adding 4 RBI and a homer. Dillon stayed hot all game at 5-for-5 with 3 RBI, and Trevor chipped in at 4-for-5 with 3 RBI, while Brandon drove in 4 runs on a 3-for-4 day. With this much offense up and down the lineup, the Invaders had enough cushion to hold on despite a high-scoring push from the Marinaders, closing out a wild, well-earned win.",
